{"id": "1542046573624561665", "channel_id": "1541789569060438036", "author_id": "1355724968956002314", "author_name": "xyakoto", "content": "modern apps and games usually support changing language on the fly, by putting all texts in a dedicated place.\nby adding tags for each words and sentences, apps/games can automatically find corresponding text via tags.\n\nfor example:\n__caraboo says: \"This is an apple\".__\nwith i18n methods it becomes:\n__caraboo says: \"sentence_1\"__\n\nsomewhere in the dedicated text file:\n** tag: sentence_1 **\nEN: \"This is an apple\"\nCN: \"这是一个苹果\"\n\nYou see this is more than just a localization problem. By centralizing all texts in one place, writers can easily change things as they want. They no longer need to dig into the game file somewhere to find what they wanna change. It makes writer works faster and more efficient. Easier to proofread, no more funny mistakes like the \"Kalabu\" incident.", "timestamp": "2026-08-26T05:42:32.992000+00:00", "thread_id": "1541789569060438036", "reactions": [{"emoji": "🔥", "emoji_id": null, "count": 2}], "thread_title": "V2.6.0.1 在线维护公告", "forum_channel_id": "1181135756958371881", "thread_tags": ["1181135885849346080", "1361342543970697397"]}
